{
  "_comment": [
    "T02 negative fixture corpus.",
    "Every entry is an instance that the contract MUST refuse, plus the reason it exists. docs/contracts.md:131 makes 'unknown fields are rejected by default' a contract term, and docs/contracts.md:19/98 fix the money and target-service rules; this file is what turns those sentences into something a test can fail on.",
    "The freeze script asserts each one is rejected by the schema named by its section, so a fixture cannot quietly become acceptable. If one of these starts passing, the protocol regressed: fix the schema, do not delete the entry.",
    "Note the deliberate absence of format-only cases for fields whose schema has no other constraint: Python's jsonschema skips 'format' unless a checker is registered, so a case that only violates 'format' would pass vacuously. _schemaio.py registers an explicit date-time checker so the date-time cases below are real."
  ],
  "execution_command": {
    "unknown-field": {
      "why": "additionalProperties:false. An unlisted member means the two sides disagree about the message shape; accepting it would let a producer smuggle a field past the consumer's validation.",
      "instance": {
